* =============================================================================
* Power Distribution Network (PDN) Decoupling - GPU Core
* =============================================================================
* Target: 0.85V rail @ 100A with <100mV droop
* Target impedance: Ztarget = Vdroop/Imax = 0.1V/100A = 1mOhm
* Target: 0.85mOhm for margin
*
* Capacitor hierarchy:
* - Bulk: 2 x 680uF SP-CAP (Panasonic)
* - Mid-frequency: 8 x 22uF MLCC (X7R, 0805)
* - High-frequency: 24 x 1uF MLCC (X7R, 0402)
* - On-die: 100nF effective
* =============================================================================

.title "GPU Core PDN Decoupling Network - Impedance Analysis"

* =============================================================================
* PARAMETERS
* =============================================================================
.param ZTARGET   = 0.85m        ; Target impedance (ohms)
.param VCORE     = 0.85         ; Core voltage (V)
.param ISTEP     = 50           ; Load step current (A)
.param T_RISE    = 1n           ; Load step rise time (s)

* PCB parasitics
.param L_VIA     = 0.5n         ; Via inductance (H)
.param R_PLANE   = 0.1m         ; Power plane resistance (ohms)
.param L_PLANE   = 0.1n         ; Power plane inductance (H)

* =============================================================================
* IMPEDANCE ANALYSIS SOURCE
* =============================================================================
* AC current source for impedance sweep
I_AC VCORE_PDN 0 AC 1

* =============================================================================
* VOLTAGE REGULATOR MODULE (VRM) OUTPUT IMPEDANCE
* =============================================================================
* The VRM presents low impedance at low frequencies
* Modeled as voltage source with output impedance

* VRM output resistance
R_VRM VRM_OUT VCORE_PDN 0.5m

* VRM output inductance (bulk capacitors dominate below crossover)
L_VRM VRM_OUT VCORE_PDN 10n

* =============================================================================
* BULK CAPACITORS (Low Frequency)
* =============================================================================
* 2 x Panasonic SP-CAP 680uF, 2V, ESR ~4mOhm each
* Effective: 1360uF, 2mOhm ESR

* Bulk capacitor 1
C_BULK1 VCORE_PDN 0 680u Rser=4m Lser=2n

* Bulk capacitor 2
C_BULK2 VCORE_PDN 0 680u Rser=4m Lser=2n

* =============================================================================
* MID-FREQUENCY CAPACITORS (22uF MLCC, 0805)
* =============================================================================
* 8 x 22uF X7R, 0805, ESR ~2mOhm each, ESL ~0.5nH each
* Distributed around the GPU package

C_MID1 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID2 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID3 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID4 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID5 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID6 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID7 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n
C_MID8 VCORE_PDN 0 22u Rser=2m Lser=0.5n

* =============================================================================
* HIGH-FREQUENCY CAPACITORS (1uF MLCC, 0402)
* =============================================================================
* 24 x 1uF X7R, 0402, ESR ~5mOhm each, ESL ~0.3nH each
* Placed directly under GPU BGA package

C_HF1 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF2 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF3 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF4 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF5 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF6 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF7 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF8 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF9 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF10 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF11 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF12 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF13 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF14 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF15 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF16 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF17 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF18 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF19 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF20 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF21 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF22 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF23 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n
C_HF24 VCORE_PDN 0 1u Rser=5m Lser=0.3n

* =============================================================================
* ON-DIE DECOUPLING
* =============================================================================
* GPU die has distributed capacitance
* Modeled as capacitor with very low ESL

R_PKG VCORE_PDN DIE_NODE {R_PLANE}
L_PKG VCORE_PDN DIE_NODE {L_PLANE}

* On-die capacitance (100nF effective)
C_DIE DIE_NODE 0 100n Rser=1m Lser=10p

* =============================================================================
* LOAD MODEL FOR TRANSIENT
* =============================================================================
* Current step for transient response testing
I_LOAD_TRAN VCORE_PDN 0 PWL(
+ 0 0
+ 1u 0
+ 1.01u {ISTEP}
+ 5u {ISTEP}
+ 5.01u 0
+ 10u 0
+)

* =============================================================================
* IMPEDANCE MEASUREMENT
* =============================================================================
* The impedance is Z = V / I (with I_AC = 1A, Z = V)
* Already connected: I_AC injects current, measure voltage at VCORE_PDN

* Target impedance reference
B_ZTARGET ZTARGET_NODE 0 V={ZTARGET}

* =============================================================================
* ANALYSIS COMMANDS
* =============================================================================
* AC analysis for impedance vs frequency
* Sweep from 100Hz to 1GHz
.AC DEC 100 100 1G

* Transient analysis for load step response
.TRAN 0 10u 0 10p

* Operating point
.OP

* Save key nodes for plotting
.SAVE V(VCORE_PDN) V(DIE_NODE) I(I_AC)
.SAVE V(ZTARGET_NODE)

* =============================================================================
* DESIGN NOTES
* =============================================================================
* PDN Design Methodology:
* 1. Calculate target impedance: Ztarget = Vdroop_max / Istep
*    Ztarget = 100mV / 100A = 1mOhm
*    Design for 0.85mOhm for margin
*
* 2. VRM provides low impedance up to ~10kHz (control loop bandwidth)
*
* 3. Bulk capacitors (680uF SP-CAP) cover 10kHz to 100kHz
*    - Large capacitance handles low-frequency transients
*    - Low ESR minimizes resistive voltage drop
*
* 4. Mid-frequency MLCC (22uF) covers 100kHz to 10MHz
*    - Fills gap between bulk and high-frequency caps
*    - 0805 package has moderate ESL
*
* 5. High-frequency MLCC (1uF, 0402) covers 10MHz to 100MHz
*    - Small package minimizes ESL
*    - Placed close to load for minimal inductance
*
* 6. On-die capacitance covers >100MHz
*    - Transistors and interconnect provide natural capacitance
*    - Closest to current consumption (zero distance)
*
* Impedance Profile:
* - DC to 10kHz: VRM control, ~0.5mOhm
* - 10kHz to 100kHz: Bulk caps dominate
* - 100kHz to 10MHz: Mid-frequency MLCC
* - 10MHz to 100MHz: High-frequency MLCC
* - >100MHz: On-die capacitance
*
* Parallel Resonances:
* - Occur when capacitor ESL resonates with next level capacitance
* - Must keep anti-resonance peaks below Ztarget
* - Achieved by overlapping capacitance values
*
* Placement Guidelines:
* - Bulk caps: Near VRM output
* - 22uF MLCC: Around GPU package perimeter
* - 1uF MLCC: Directly under GPU BGA (via-in-pad)
* - Minimize loop area for each capacitor
*
* PCB Stackup:
* - Use multiple power/ground plane pairs
* - Keep power and ground planes close (2-3 mil dielectric)
* - Minimize plane spreading inductance
* =============================================================================

.END
